23:T4e5,Most rejected proposals fail in the same place: the research question. Not because the topic is uninteresting, but because the question is unanswerable, unmeasurable, or already answered.

## Topic, problem, question

A topic is a subject area. A problem is a tension inside that area — something unresolved, contradictory or unmeasured. A question is a specific, testable formulation of that tension.

- Topic: remote work and productivity.
- Problem: studies disagree on the direction and size of the effect.
- Question: under which task types does remote work change measured output for knowledge workers?

## Three filters

1. **Reachability** — can you obtain the data, sample or documents within your timeframe?
2. **Measurability** — is there a defensible operational definition for each construct?
3. **Contribution** — if answered, does something change for a reader, a policy or a field?

> A question that passes two filters is a chapter. A question that passes three is a thesis.

## Then reverse-engineer the method

Once the question is fixed, the methodology writes itself: the design follows the question type, the sample follows the population, the analysis follows the construct definitions. That is the order reviewers expect.16:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","$L20",null,{"title":"Blog","desc":"Create, edit, schedule and publish articles. Language + Audience + Access + Status are independent fields."}],["$","$L21",null,{"configured":false}],["$","$L22",null,{"rows":[{"id":"p_research-question-that-survives-review","slug":"research-question-that-survives-review","title":{"en":"Designing a Research Question That Survives Review","ne":"समीक्षा टिक्ने अनुसन्धान प्रश्न कसरी बनाउने"},"excerpt":{"en":"A research question is not a topic. It is a claim about what is unknown, why it matters, and how it can be answered with the data you can actually reach.","ne":"अनुसन्धान प्रश्न विषय होइन। यो के अज्ञात छ, किन महत्त्वपूर्ण छ, र कुन डाटाले उत्तर दिन सकिन्छ भन्ने दाबी हो।"},"content":{"en":"$23","ne":"धेरैजसो अस्वीकृत प्रस्ताव एउटै ठाउँमा असफल हुन्छन्: अनुसन्धान प्रश्न। विषय कमजोर भएकोले होइन, प्रश्न अनुत्तरणीय, अपरिमेय वा पहिल्यै उत्तरित भएकोले।\n\n## विषय, समस्या, प्रश्न\n\nविषय एउटा क्षेत्र हो। समस्या त्यस क्षेत्रभित्रको तनाव हो। प्रश्न त्यस तनावको विशिष्ट र परीक्षणयोग्य रूप हो।\n\n## तीन फिल्टर\n\n1. **पहुँच** — तोकिएको समयमा डाटा वा नमूना प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ?\n2. **मापनयोग्यता** — प्रत्येक कन्स्ट्रक्टको रक्षा गर्न सकिने परिभाषा छ?\n3. **योगदान** — उत्तर मिलेमा पाठक, नीति वा क्षेत्रमा केही परिवर्तन हुन्छ?\n\n> दुई फिल्टर पास गर्ने प्रश्न एउटा अध्याय हो। तीनै पास गर्ने प्रश्न थेसिस हो।"},"cover":"art:research","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Research","tags":["methodology","proposal","thesis"],"publishedAt":"2026-09-17","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"public","audience":"global","featured":true,"seoTitle":"Designing a Research Question That Survives Review | Acttolog","seoDescription":"A research question is not a topic. It is a claim about what is unknown, why it matters, and how it can be answered with the data you can actually reach.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/research-question-that-survives-review"},{"id":"p_reproducible-data-analysis-workflow","slug":"reproducible-data-analysis-workflow","title":{"en":"A Practical Workflow for Reproducible Data Analysis","ne":"पुनरुत्पादनयोग्य डाटा विश्लेषणको व्यावहारिक वर्कफ्लो"},"excerpt":{"en":"Reproducibility is a time-saving strategy: the person you are protecting is future you, three weeks from now, under deadline.","ne":"पुनरुत्पादनशीलता समय बचाउने रणनीति हो: तपाईंले जोगाउन खोज्नुभएको व्यक्ति तीन हप्तापछिको तपाईं नै हुनुहुन्छ।"},"content":{"en":"Reproducible analysis means someone else — or you, later — can start from raw data and arrive at the same numbers without asking a single question.\n\n## The five-folder structure\n\n- `01_raw` — untouched source files, read-only.\n- `02_clean` — cleaning scripts and their outputs.\n- `03_analysis` — models, tests, figures.\n- `04_output` — tables and charts used in the document.\n- `05_docs` — data dictionary, decisions log, environment file.\n\n## Never edit raw data by hand\n\nEvery transformation lives in a script. If a value is wrong in the source, record the correction in the script with a reason.\n\n## Keep a decisions log\n\nOne plain text file, appended chronologically: date, decision, reason, alternative rejected. This single file answers most examiner questions before they are asked.\n\n> If a number appears in your document, a script must be able to produce it from files in `01_raw`.","ne":"पुनरुत्पादनयोग्य विश्लेषणको अर्थ — अर्को व्यक्तिले (वा पछि तपाईंले) कच्चा डाटाबाट सुरु गरेर एउटै सङ्ख्यामा पुग्न सक्नु, एउटा पनि प्रश्न नसोधी।\n\n## पाँच फोल्डर संरचना\n\n- `01_raw` — नछोइएको स्रोत फाइल।\n- `02_clean` — सफाइ स्क्रिप्ट र नतिजा।\n- `03_analysis` — मोडेल, परीक्षण, चित्र।\n- `04_output` — कागजातमा प्रयोग भएका तालिका र चार्ट।\n- `05_docs` — डाटा शब्दकोश, निर्णय लग, इन्भाइरोन्मेन्ट फाइल।\n\n> कागजातमा देखिने हरेक सङ्ख्या `01_raw` बाट स्क्रिप्टले बनाउन सक्नुपर्छ।"},"cover":"art:editorial","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Technology","tags":["data","workflow"],"publishedAt":"2026-09-12","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"public","audience":"global","featured":false,"seoTitle":"A Practical Workflow for Reproducible Data Analysis | Acttolog","seoDescription":"Reproducibility is a time-saving strategy: the person you are protecting is future you, three weeks from now, under deadline.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/reproducible-data-analysis-workflow"},{"id":"p_thesis-chapter-structure-reviewers-trust","slug":"thesis-chapter-structure-reviewers-trust","title":{"en":"How to Structure a Thesis Chapter Reviewers Trust","ne":"समीक्षकले पत्याउने थेसिस अध्याय संरचना"},"excerpt":{"en":"Reviewers reward predictability: a chapter that says where it is, what it does and what it concluded.","ne":"समीक्षकले पूर्वानुमानयोग्यतालाई पुरस्कृत गर्छन्: अध्यायले आफू कहाँ छ, के गर्छ र के निष्कर्ष निकाल्यो भन्नुपर्छ।"},"content":{"en":"A trustworthy chapter has a visible skeleton. The reader should be able to skim headings alone and understand the argument.\n\n## The standard spine\n\n1. Purpose of the chapter, stated in the first paragraph.\n2. Structure signpost — what follows and in what order.\n3. Body sections, each with one job.\n4. Synthesis — what the sections mean together.\n5. Bridge — how this chapter sets up the next one.\n\n## One job per section\n\nIf a section is doing two things, split it. Reviewers flag sprawl faster than they flag brevity.\n\n> Clarity is a form of rigour. If a reader has to guess your structure, they will assume you guessed it too.","ne":"विश्वासिलो अध्यायको कङ्काल देखिन्छ। पाठकले शीर्षक मात्र पढेर पनि तर्क बुझ्नुपर्छ।\n\n## मानक संरचना\n\n1. अध्यायको उद्देश्य, पहिलो प्याराग्राफमै।\n2. संरचना संकेत — आगे के आउँछ, कुन क्रममा।\n3. मुख्य खण्ड, प्रत्येकको एउटै काम।\n4. संश्लेषण — सबै खण्ड मिलेर् अर्थ के।\n5. पुल — यो अध्यायले अर्कोलाई कसरी तयार गर्छ।\n\n> स्पष्टता पनि कठोरताकै रूप हो।"},"cover":"art:academy","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Education","tags":["thesis","writing"],"publishedAt":"2026-09-06","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"members","audience":"global","featured":false,"seoTitle":"How to Structure a Thesis Chapter Reviewers Trust | Acttolog","seoDescription":"Reviewers reward predictability: a chapter that says where it is, what it does and what it concluded.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/thesis-chapter-structure-reviewers-trust"},{"id":"p_storytelling-systems-creativity-data","slug":"storytelling-systems-creativity-data","title":{"en":"Storytelling Systems: Where Creativity Meets Data","ne":"कथा प्रणाली: सिर्जनशीलता र डाटाको सङ्गम"},"excerpt":{"en":"The strongest media work treats data as a constraint generator and creativity as the search space.","ne":"बलियो मिडिया कार्यले डाटालाई सिमाना निर्माता र सिर्जनशीलतालाई खोज क्षेत्र मान्छ।"},"content":{"en":"Creativity and data are usually presented as opposites. In practice, the strongest media work treats data as a constraint generator and creativity as the search space.\n\n## Constraints accelerate invention\n\nA blank page is slow. A rule is fast. Give a story a fixed runtime, a limited palette, a single location, and decisions collapse into a manageable set.\n\n## Measure one thing\n\nRetention, completion, rewatch or beat placement — pick one signal per project. Multiple signals produce multiple contradictory edits.\n\n## Build a feedback loop\n\n- Produce a small unit of work.\n- Release it to a limited audience.\n- Record the signal and the qualitative note.\n- Change exactly one variable.\n\nThis is why Acttolog keeps research and entertainment inside the same world.","ne":"सिर्जनशीलता र डाटालाई प्रायः विपरित मानिन्छ। व्यवहारमा बलियो मिडिया कार्यले डाटालाई सिमाना निर्माता र सिर्जनशीलतालाई खोज क्षेत्र मान्छ।\n\n## सिमानाले आविष्कार छिटो बनाउँछ\n\nखाली पृष्ठ ढिलो हुन्छ। नियम छिटो हुन्छ। कथालाई निश्चित समय, सीमित प्यालेट र एउटै स्थान दिनुहोस् — निर्णयहरू व्यवस्थापनयोग्य बन्छन्।\n\nयसैले Acttolog ले अनुसन्धान र मनोरञ्जनलाई एउटै संसारमा राख्छ।"},"cover":"art:music","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Creativity","tags":["storytelling","media"],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"public","audience":"global","featured":false,"seoTitle":"Storytelling Systems: Where Creativity Meets Data | Acttolog","seoDescription":"The strongest media work treats data as a constraint generator and creativity as the search space.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/storytelling-systems-creativity-data"},{"id":"p_immersive-web-design-notes","slug":"immersive-web-design-notes","title":{"en":"Building a Digital World: Notes on Immersive Web Design","ne":"डिजिटल संसार निर्माण: इमर्सिभ वेब डिजाइनका टिप्पणी"},"excerpt":{"en":"A 3D hero is not decoration. It is a navigation promise about how the site expects to be explored.","ne":"3D हिरो सजावट होइन। साइट कसरी अन्वेषण गरिने भन्ने प्रतिबद्धता हो।"},"content":{"en":"Immersive web experiences fail in two predictable ways: they are slow, or they are meaningless. Both are design problems.\n\n## Performance is part of the aesthetic\n\n- Cap device pixel ratio; a 3x retina canvas is wasted work.\n- Reduce particle counts and texture resolution on small or low-core devices.\n- Pause rendering when the canvas is off-screen or the tab is hidden.\n- Honour reduced-motion preferences and offer a calm alternative.\n\n## Motion should carry information\n\nCamera movement, scroll-linked rotation and light changes should answer: where am I, and what just changed? Motion that only decorates becomes noise within seconds.\n\n## Progressive depth\n\nLoad the shell first, then the world. A visitor should be able to read, navigate and act before the 3D layer finishes warming up.\n\n> The entrance to a digital world should feel like an arrival, not a loading screen.","ne":"इमर्सिभ वेब अनुभव दुई अनुमानित तरिकाले असफल हुन्छन्: ढिलो, वा अर्थहीन। दुवै डिजाइन समस्या हुन्।\n\n## परफर्मेन्स पनि सौन्दर्यकै भाग हो\n\n- डिभाइस पिक्सेल रेसियो सीमित राख्नुहोस्।\n- साना वा कमजोर यन्त्रमा पार्टिकल र टेक्सचर घटाउनुहोस्।\n- क्यानभास बाहिर जाँदा वा ट्याब लुक्दा रेन्डरिङ रोक्नुहोस्।\n- रिड्युस्ड-मोसन प्राथमिकता सम्मान गर्नुहोस्।\n\n> डिजिटल संसारको प्रवेशद्वार आगमन जस्तो हुनुपर्छ, लोडिङ स्क्रिन जस्तो होइन।"},"cover":"art:nebula","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Media","tags":["webgl","design","performance"],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"public","audience":"global","featured":true,"seoTitle":"Building a Digital World: Notes on Immersive Web Design | Acttolog","seoDescription":"A 3D hero is not decoration. It is a navigation promise about how the site expects to be explored.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/immersive-web-design-notes"},{"id":"p_darkroom-verification-philosophy","slug":"darkroom-verification-philosophy","title":{"en":"Why Darkroom Publishes No Popularity Numbers","ne":"डार्करूमले लोकप्रियता सङ्ख्या किन देखाउँदैन"},"excerpt":{"en":"A resource list ranked by clicks rewards whoever marketed hardest, not whoever is most useful.","ne":"क्लिकका आधारमा क्रमबद्ध सूचीले सबैभन्दा बढी प्रचार गर्नेलाई पुरस्कृत गर्छ, सबैभन्दा उपयोगीलाई होइन।"},"content":{"en":"A resource list ranked by clicks rewards whoever marketed hardest, not whoever is most useful. Darkroom takes a different position.\n\n## Discover → Verify → Organize → Access\n\nEvery important resource carries: what it is, why it is useful, who it is for, where it leads, official status, pricing type and review status. That is more work than a link list, and it is the point.\n\n## Why popularity stays private\n\nPublic view counts create feedback loops. A resource that is already ahead gets clicked more, ranks higher and pushes better alternatives down. Acttolog keeps usage signals inside Acttolog Intelligence where they inform maintenance — detecting broken links and stale reviews — instead of steering public attention.\n\n## Status labels instead of stars\n\nOfficial · Verified · Needs Review · Broken · Suspicious. No star ratings, no public written reviews, no trending badges.\n\n> If a resource deserves attention, the reason should be written down.","ne":"क्लिकका आधारमा क्रमबद्ध सूचीले सबैभन्दा बढी प्रचार गर्नेलाई पुरस्कृत गर्छ, सबैभन्दा उपयोगीलाई होइन। डार्करूमले फरक बाटो लिन्छ।\n\n## खोज → प्रमाणीकरण → व्यवस्थापन → पहुँच\n\nहरेक महत्त्वपूर्ण स्रोतसँग हुन्छ: यो के हो, किन उपयोगी छ, कसका लागि हो, कहाँ पुर्‍याउँछ, आधिकारिक स्थिति, मूल्य प्रकार र समीक्षा स्थिति।\n\n## तारा होइन, स्थिति लेबल\n\nआधिकारिक · प्रमाणित · समीक्षा आवश्यक · बिग्रिएको · शंकास्पद।"},"cover":"art:editorial","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Media","tags":["darkroom","trust"],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"public","audience":"global","featured":false,"seoTitle":"Why Darkroom Publishes No Popularity Numbers | Acttolog","seoDescription":"A resource list ranked by clicks rewards whoever marketed hardest, not whoever is most useful.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/darkroom-verification-philosophy"},{"id":"p_members-research-checklist","slug":"members-research-checklist","title":{"en":"Members: The Pre-Submission Research Checklist","ne":"सदस्य: पेश अघिको अनुसन्धान चेकलिस्ट"},"excerpt":{"en":"A members-only checklist covering structure, citations, similarity review, figures, tables and the final consistency pass.","ne":"संरचना, उद्धरण, सिमिलारिटी समीक्षा, चित्र, तालिका र अन्तिम एकरूपता जाँच समेटिएको सदस्य-विशेष चेकलिस्ट।"},"content":{"en":"This article is available to signed-in members.\n\n## Before you submit\n\n- Every chapter opens with purpose and closes with a bridge.\n- Every table and figure is referenced in the text and numbered sequentially.\n- Every citation in the text appears in the reference list, and vice versa.\n- Similarity report reviewed section by section, with problem areas identified.\n- AI-related review completed and documented.\n- Formatting matches the institutional template exactly — margins, fonts, heading levels.\n- Analysis outputs reproducible from raw data using the stored scripts.\n\n> A checklist does not replace judgement. It prevents judgement from being spent on things that were already solved.","ne":"यो लेख साइन-इन सदस्यहरूका लागि उपलब्ध छ।\n\n## पेश गर्नुअघि\n\n- हरेक अध्याय उद्देश्यबाट सुरु र पुलबाट अन्त्य हुन्छ।\n- हरेक तालिका र चित्र पाठमा उल्लेख र क्रमबद्ध छन्।\n- पाठका हरेक उद्धरण सन्दर्भ सूचीमा छन्, र उल्टो पनि।\n- सिमिलारिटी प्रतिवेदन खण्ड अनुसार समीक्षा गरिएको छ।\n- फर्माटिङ संस्थागत टेम्प्लेटसँग ठ्याक्कै मिल्छ।"},"cover":"art:academy","author":"Acttolog Editorial","category":"Research","tags":["checklist","members"],"publishedAt":"2026-09-20","updatedAt":"","status":"published","access":"members","audience":"global","featured":false,"seoTitle":"Members: The Pre-Submission Research Checklist | Acttolog","seoDescription":"A members-only checklist covering structure, citations, similarity review, figures, tables and the final consistency pass.","socialImage":"","__href":"/blog/members-research-checklist"}],"cols":[{"key":"title","label":"Title"},{"key":"category","label":"Category"},{"key":"status","label":"Status"},{"key":"access","label":"Access"},{"key":"publishedAt","label":"Published"},{"key":"author","label":"Author"}]}]]}],null,"$L24"]}]
